(ARG-21 — `with default <value>` initializes the flag when it is not
 passed (LANGUAGE.md:4756, 4760). Run with no arguments, so every
 default is the value observed. The manual shows a text default only;
 number and boolean defaults are accepted too and are included here.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-21.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   output is out.txt
   retries is 7
   loud is 1
)
a flag called output is "-o" or "--output", it is a text with default "out.txt".
a flag called retries is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number with default 7.
a flag called loud is "-l" or "--loud", it is a boolean with default true.
Parse flags.

Print "output is {output}".
Print "retries is {retries}".
Print "loud is {loud}".
